Requirement Text HRS E0383388 01 _ REV 2:
If an angular movement to be requested to the ST is beyond the specified limits:
• The ST shall saturate the command to be generated to the closest permitted limit value;
• The ST shall send to the Coral Mainframe reporting of the limitation applied.

The BIT function shall include at least the verification of the following aspects:
• Temperature and current monitoring sensors;
• Input voltage to the ST modules;
• Interfaces towards the Turret and the Coral Mainframe.

The ST shall support the following operative states:
• INIT: at the Power-On;
• FAIL: in case of Turret and/or CU non-correct functioning (see the Requirement [624427]);
• MAINTENANCE: for Self-Levelling, IBIT, and activities on the Testing Interface (see the Requirement [624715]);
• OPERATIONAL: The turret and CU operate normally (e.g., steering the Turret in the desired direction);
• SAFE: when all the moving/rotating elements of the Turret are locked for safety reasons.

The ST shall enter the Fail State if any of the following conditions hold:
The PBIT, CBIT, or IBIT do not provide positive results or not terminate within their own "time-out" period;
A failure signal is received.
Any step of the Self-Levelling operation does not terminate within its own "time-out" period;
Activities on the Testing Interface do not terminate within their own "time-out" period.

The state transitions of the ST shall be commanded by the ST Manager CSCI with the only exceptions of the following ones:
Entry into the Init State;
Entry into the Fail State;
Entry into the Safe State from the Init State.

In the Maintenance State, the ST shall be allowed to carry out the following operations:
•Self-Levelling;
•Setting of the flag for internal/external automatic tracking indication;
•Identification of the source (among the two available) in case of external automatic tracking.

Note: See the Requirement [624353] for the definition of the two external tracking sources.

The ST CSCI Manager Interface shall:
Send aggregated BIT results;
Send Safety checks (Safe Condition Indication);
Receive Transition State Commands;
Receive Movements Commands deriving from the automatic tracking;
Receive Operational State Modes setting.
